## Why This Is Asked
This question probes ability to design multi-protocol contract governance, versioning, and cross-protocol mappings in a real product. It tests practical approaches to keep REST, GraphQL, and gRPC synchronized, handle migrations with minimal disruption, and implement tests and observability.

## Key Concepts
- Single source of truth for OpenAPI, SDL, and proto contracts
- Versioned envelopes and per-endpoint migrations
- Deprecation windows and non-breaking changes
- Cross-protocol mappings (REST -> GraphQL -> gRPC)
- Consumer-driven contract tests, validation, and observability (tracing/metrics)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal versioned contract envelope
class ContractEnvelope {
  constructor(version, restOpenAPI, graphqlSDL, grpcProto) {
    this.version = version;
    this.rest = restOpenAPI;
    this.graphql = graphqlSDL;
    this.grpc = grpcProto;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you automate contract generation and validation across all three protocols?
- How would you handle breaking changes and feature flag migrations without affecting existing clients?
- What testing strategy would you use to ensure cross-protocol semantics stay in sync over time?

