## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design cross-cache invalidation for multi-tenant scales with Redis as the source of truth and Memcached as a secondary layer. Requires concrete event schemas, per-tenant isolation, and practical guards against stale reads.

## Key Concepts

- Cache-invalidation workflow across Redis and Memcached with tenant isolation
- Event schema design (tenantId, articleId, version) and idempotent handling
- Stampede protection (hot-key guards, probabilistic refresh) and recovery strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Redis publish invalidation event
function publishInvalidation(tenantId, articleId, newVersion) {
  const event = { tenantId, articleId, version: newVersion, timestamp: Date.now() };
  redis.publish('cache:invalidate', JSON.stringify(event));
}

// Redis listener and Memcached worker
function handleInvalidation(event) {
  const key = `article:${event.tenantId}:${event.articleId}`;
  redis.del(key);
  redis.incr(`version:${event.tenantId}`);

  // Memcached CAS invalidation
  memcached.gets(key, (err, data, cas) => {
    if (data) memcached.cas(key, '', cas, 0, () => {});
  });
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates cache invalidation strategies at scale, per-tenant data isolation, and stampede protection mechanisms in Redis-based systems. It also tests understanding of Pub/Sub invalidation patterns and lightweight locking approaches.

## Key Concepts

- Write-through cache architecture
- Per-tenant TTL management and version stamping
- Distributed locking to prevent cache stampede
- Pub/Sub-based invalidation and out-of-band refresh
- Performance trade-offs: data freshness vs. system load

## Code Example

```javascript
async function getProduct(id, tenant) {
  const cacheKey = `prod:${tenant}:${id}`;
  let data = await redis.get(cacheKey);
  if (data) return JSON.parse(data);

  const lockKey = `${cacheKey}:lock`;
  const lock = await redis.set(lockKey, '1', 'PX', 5000, 'NX');

  if (lock) {
    try {
      const freshData = await fetchFromDB(id, tenant);
      await redis.setex(cacheKey, 300, JSON.stringify(freshData));
      return freshData;
    } finally {
      await redis.del(lockKey);
    }
  }

  await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));
  return getProduct(id, tenant);
}
```

